      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Browser and API",
      "items": [
        "Node.js serves the dashboard assets and handles browser HTTP requests.",
        "The dashboard polls availability, events and history every five seconds.",
        "An optional timer in the parking service generates simulated visits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Native bridge",
      "items": [
        "Node.js owns one persistent Python child process and matches NDJSON responses by request ID.",
        "Python serializes operations and invokes the Java client through JPype.",
        "Replies return through the same bridge; GridDB operations use its native protocol."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Data and scope",
      "items": [
        "Collections store spaces, sessions and events; TimeSeries store occupancy and per-space projections.",
        "Sessions are authoritative; projection writes are separate and can return warnings.",
        "Native-mode overview. The optional in-memory demo bypasses Python and GridDB."
      ]
    }
  ]
